\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 / \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  -3: Some Allege Market Manipulation \b0\par\par\uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 1996\par 14:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Economics professor Salih Neftci voiced a belief that's widespread among market players by writing in the Sunday edition of daily newspaper Hurriyet that market-makers, in coordination with the government, are buying and selling bills and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Treasury, \par \par \uc2  Some onlookers allege that a political alliance between certain market participants and the government, the weight of state-owned banks' portfolios and the vested interests of major private banks participating in the Treasury-bill market increase the possibility of manipulation in this week's auctions. \par \par \uc2  'This time, manipulation by market-makers will have weight,' said Tezan of Bank Kapital. 'Five months ago, under the same market conditions, they would leave the market.' \par \par \uc2  Some interpret the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an indication of the government's desire to move to a controlled economy, also citing a recent attempt to fix bread prices. \par \par \uc2  'We'll see this week if the government wants to print money,' said Ipek of Garanti Investment. 'But controls and anxious markets won't help anyone. Then foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumps, stocks crash. I hope and I wish no such thing happens. But I'm not absolutely certain - it's a wish.' \par \par \uc2  Players also said it's hard to make sense of the moves when the government remains idle on the deficit front, but is actively trying to curb interest rates. \par \par \uc2  'The next test after this is the November inflation data,' Tezan said. 'Current structure means fundamentals will always pressure the rates.' \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 11-11-96 \par \par \uc2  1321GMT \par \par \uc2  1146 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dsbb00v57\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
