\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 's Lira Dn Vs Dollar; Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Speculated \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 1996\par 16:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (AP-Dow Jones)--The Turkish lira closed lower against the dollar Wednesday following a day of dollar buying demand from individual buyers, which also fueled demand at the interbank market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they suspect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars incognito Wednesday at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -guided \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Lower asking quotes are usually attributed to the bank on the assumption that profit driven commercial banks wouldn't sell dollars below the going market rate. \par \par \uc2  Turkey's parliament started debating the opposition's no-confidence motion against the government after the market closed. Traders said they expect the government to stay on and saw no connection between the recent exchange- rate movements and the political situation. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar's international gains were reflected on the lira and man on the street sees it as -dollar is going up, so let's buy- opportunity,' said Ziynet Sancili, dealer at Sumerbank AS in Istanbul, adding that dollar demand could also come from importers. \par \par \uc2  At 1200 GMT the dollar closed at 94,700 lira on the interbank market, up from Tuesday's 94,500 lira. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar buying rate for commercial banks' minimum reserves was at 94,150 lira, up from 93,950 lira. A trader said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar selling began at 94,780 lira and continued until 94,660 lira. \par \par \uc2  Around 1218 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 1.5407 Deutsche marks, up from 1.5403 marks in London around 1035 GMT and from 1.5405 marks in New York late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said a flurry of statements from the government on treasury bill auctions also confuse the market and this could prompt lira t-bill positions to switch into dollars, although no such move is seen yet. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-10-96 \par \par \uc2  1458GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 1862 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dsag003il\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
