\par\par \b \uc2  Turkish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  acts to hold jittery mkts. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tulin Aygunes \par \uc2 729 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL,  July 18 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , t-bill and money markets this week to maintain control amid jitters over economic policies of the new Islamist-led government, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were effective in easing the immediate shocks in the markets, but this can't last forever, (\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar) buying must ease," said Bora Cilek, assistant general manager at Midland Bank's Istanbul branch. \par \par \uc2  The bank sold dollars for lira to banks and free market dealers for the fourth day in a row to curtail the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise despite the dollar's weakness on world markets. \par \par \uc2  It also raised its overnight bid and offer rates to 50-80 percent on Thursday from Wednesday's 45-75 to support the lira. \par \par \uc2  Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the lira closed weaker at 83,110 per dollar after Wednesday's 82,920. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, weighted 40 percent dollar and 60 percent mark, gained 1.02 percent against the lira so far this week after 0.8 percent last week. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also bought overnight repos and t-bills from time to time this week to control rates. \par \par \uc2  T-bill yields have surged between 12 and 15 percentage points since last Thursday when Islamist finance minister Abdullatif Sener suggested capping domestic borrowing interest rates and introducing new taxes on t-bills and bonds. \par \par \uc2  Sener, speaking during a parliamentary debate on means to boost state revenues, also forecast 1996 budget deficit at 1,300 trillion lira, up sharply from an official target of 861 trillion due to hefty domestic debt servicing. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Necmettin Erbakan repeated on Tuesday assurances given on Monday by Deputy Premier Tansu Ciller and her conservative ministers that the government did not plan any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in free market economy. \par \par \uc2  But conservative State Minister Ufuk Soylemez confirmed government plans on new taxes on t-bills and bonds by saying a withholding tax to be introduced would not be retroactive. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the t-bill market anxiously awaited clarification by the government on withholding tax plans as well as a solid programme to fight the country's huge budget deficit. \par \par \uc2  Economists and bankers question the coalition's ability to finance an additional 125 trillion lira burden from a 50 percent civil servant pay rise for second half 1996. \par \par \uc2  Erbakan said on Thursday the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was stable and predicted interest rates would fall gradually. \par \par \uc2  Talking at his Islamist Welfare Party meeting, Erbakan reiterated plans to use untapped resources to finance government projects including the pay rises. \par \par \uc2  The coalition expects a 300 trillion lira income from the planned sale of properties and buildings, Ciller said on Tuesday, but did not give a time span. She added that the tax base would be widened, but tax rates would not be increased. \par \par \uc2  "The increase in overnight rates and speculation over the treasury's heavy use of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  advances have increased anxiety in the t-bill market," said a private bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in its weekly report the treasury withdrew 83 trillion lira last week, raising its outstanding cash advances to 203 trillion. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  advances to treasury cannot exceed 326.3 trillion this year. \par \par \uc2  "Because the treasury used up most of its cash borrowing line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it must borrow in next week's t-bill auction. So the rise in interest rates may continue," the banker said. \par \par \uc2  Banks had shunned the Treasury's 204-day t-bill auction on Monday amid uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  The Treasury raised the average yield by 12 points but could sell only 16.4 trillion lira nominal bills for which it collected 10 trillion lira from banks on Tuesday, but injected 91 trillion lira for maturing t-bills in return. \par \par \uc2  Bankers also have worries ahead of Turkey ratings expected to be released by international agencies soon. \par \par \uc2  "Expectations that Turkey's outlook may be lowered and fears over how the treasury will meet its hefty domestic debt repayments in coming weeks are raising tension in the markets and putting upward pressure on the dollar," Cilek said. \par \par \uc2  The treasury faces 51 trillion lira of t-bill maturities on July 25 and 105 trillion on July 31. \par \par \uc2  -- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds7i05bcr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
