\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 's Lire Down With Demand; Cntl Bnk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 11:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (AP-Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lire fell against U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday, as demand for dollars rose and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's limited attempts to stabilize rates failed to satisfy the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A nervous buying spree for dollars this week reversed limited demand last week, with some banks posting buying rates of more than 71,000 lire Wednesday morning and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offering to sell dollars at 70,990 lire. \par \par \uc2  At 0944 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 70,800 lire, up from Tuesday's 70,590 lire, shortly after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars at 70,820 lire. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's buying rate for the minimum reserves of commercial banks rose to 70,250 lire from Tuesday's 70,150 lire. Commercial banks demanded 22.9 trillion lire from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -controlled lira interbank market, down from Tuesday's 26 trillion. \par \par \uc2  'The market prefers to stay in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as Treasury bill monthly yields of 8% match the dollar and Deutsche mark rates increase,' said a dealer who requested anonymity. \par \par \uc2  Uncertainty in the new government's monetary policy and Tuesday's data regarding a 1995 trade deficit that rose by 172.5% and short dollar positions of the banks appear to be leading demand. Also, the dollar's rise on international markets isn't helping the lira. \par \par \uc2  'There are no sellers, and only buyers,' said Sema Cagatay of Egebank. 'The demand could be curbed only if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  decisively.' \par \par \uc2  Despite worries of the repetition of the 1994 crisis which was followed by an overnight devaluation, analysts said the dollar's upward trend is temporary and might be balanced by mid-April with higher T-bill rates and the start of tourism revenue and workers' remittances from Europe. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-03-96 \par \par \uc2  1051GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds3r02pgd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
