\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 's Lira Down With Demand;  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 12:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ISTANBUL (AP-Dow Jones)--The Turkish lira is down against the dollar Friday as demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues amid uncertainty over the monetary policies of the new coalition government. \par \par \uc2  Demand for the U.S. dollar is partly seen due to a 'crowd effect,' the move by banks to follow each other in buying the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Besides, some banks are keen on covering short positions, which are no longer attractive, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  After spotting some banks' demand for the dollar Friday morning, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called these banks and offered to sell them dollars, prompting a curb in demand and keeping its reserve loss to a minimum. \par \par \uc2  At 0950 GMT, the dollar was traded at 69,910 lira, up from Thursday's 69,530 lira. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has increased its dollar buying rate for banks' minimum reserves to 69,310 lira from 69,230 lira. The market opened with banks' requests for 60 trillion lira from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'The dollar increase has been higher than those of the borrowing rates,' said Emrah Aksaray of ABN Amro Bank in Istanbul 'This was regarded as correction. But the increase can't go on with this rate.' \par \par \uc2  Daily increases of 50 to 60 lira in the sliding peg against the dollar is seen as 'normal', but the increase has been accelerated to a fast 150-200 lira in the last 3 weeks. \par \par \uc2  Still, some dealers see the lira's month-to-date depreciation of 5.3% against the dollar as bearable, estimating the end-March dollar rate at 70,500 to 70,600 lira, in line with 6% monthly inflation. \par \par \uc2  'The market could settle when the government's monetary policies are pronounced,' said Sevgi Aytekin of Alternatifbank AS. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 22-03-96 \par \par \uc2  1105GMT \par \par \uc2  1169 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds3m02k2t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
