\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY \highlight\uc2  '96/ \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2  Lira -4: More  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 1995\par 07:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Domestic debt has already climbed to 1.400 trillion lire, about a third of which is held by domestic banks who are fearing a refinancing crush next year and have sent the three-month Treasury annual compound rate soaring to 170%. This is the highest rate level the country has suffered since last spring when the stabilization program was first introduced. \par \par \uc2  Some fear that rates could still rise as far as 300% before the new government is formed and a new austerity program put in place. \par \par \uc2  Despite this, Xafa said, the lira remains under pressure even with this high level of interest rates, underscoring concern about the country's future and helping to worsen a merchandise trade gap that is already expected to widen to $6.5 billion this year. \par \par \uc2  At this rate, Tezan said, a devaluation could be welcomed - although it would put inflation at risk once again, it would help improve Turkey's competitiveness as it lifts barriers with Europe. \par \par \uc2  So far, though, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has showed it isn't planning to allow any swift decline. It has pumped as much as $2.5 billion of its $17 billion official reserves into the market to support the lira over the last month. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said it has also spent about $3 billion in forward dollar quotes to help cap future pressures on the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At the moment, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is quoting a rate of 63,112 lire for Feb. 2, 1996, suggesting that it sees the decline continuing around the current pace with inflation rising about 6% a month. \par \par \uc2  And a Turkish newspaper reported Monday that the IMF doesn't recomment a devaluation of the lira in 1996, preferring instead a gradual depreciation. \par \par \uc2  (This is the latest in a series of AP-Dow Jones forecasts of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market developments in 1996. A related story appears on Telerate page 1141.) \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-12-95 \par \par \uc2  0601GMT \par \par \uc2  1140 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drcj09xvx\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Turkey near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trg